cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use these notebooks or the toolbox, please cite this repository. A Tutorial article
  describing them is in preparation; this file will be updated when it appears. If you use the
  data, please also cite the RDB7 data set listed under "references".
title: "ConformalPrimer: hands-on notebooks on conformal prediction for physical chemists"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Khairbek
    given-names: "Ali A."
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0477-5896"
    affiliation: >-
      Department of Mechanical Engineering, University Centre for Research & Development,
      Chandigarh University, Gharuan, Mohali, Punjab, India
version: "0.3.0"
date-released: "2026-10-13"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/alikhairbek/ConformalPrimer"
abstract: >-
  Six self-contained Jupyter notebooks that derive conformal prediction step by step in NumPy on a
  public data set of reaction barrier heights (RDB7): split conformal prediction and the
  distribution of its coverage, CV+ and jackknife+, normalized scores and conformalized quantile
  regression, Mondrian calibration, behavior under distribution shift with weighted conformal
  prediction and recalibration, and selection with a guaranteed false discovery rate.
keywords:
  - conformal prediction
  - uncertainty quantification
  - prediction intervals
  - reaction barrier heights
  - machine learning
  - false discovery rate
  - physical chemistry
